# CODEOWNERS for the Patchwork marketplace catalogue (the `catalogue`
# branch). GitHub reads CODEOWNERS from a pull request's base branch, so this
# file governs catalogue pull requests; main's CODEOWNERS governs the
# application and the Submission paths guard.
#
# Fill this in when the branch is created (see MAINTAINERS.md, "Setup").
# Every rule must name real accounts or teams.
#
# 1. The maintainers own everything by default, including the workflows,
#    this file, moderation.json and every publisher claim:
#
#      *                         @<owner>/<maintainers-team>
#
# 2. When a namespace is registered, add its owner for its packages, so
#    their pull requests need their own approval as well as a maintainer's:
#
#      /packages/<namespace>/    @<github-login> @<owner>/<maintainers-team>
